      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most residential roof replacements in Utah take 1 to 3 days of active work, depending on the roofing material, roof size, and weather.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "1 to 3 days"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Typical Installation Timeframes by Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: 1 to 2 days for most average-sized homes."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: 2 to 5 days, depending on panel style and roof complexity."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flat Roofing: 2 to 3 days."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cedar Shake: 3 to 4 days."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Concrete, Clay, or Slate Tile: Up to 1 to 2 weeks due to weight, cutting, and installation precision.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2,
              3,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Can Lengthen the Timeline in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Weather: Snow, rain, high winds, and freezing temperatures can pause work or require waiting for dry, safe conditions\u2014especially in higher-elevation areas like Heber City and across Northern Utah.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size & Complexity: Steep pitches, multiple stories, valleys, dormers, and skylights add time.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-Off & Decking Repairs: Stripping old layers and replacing damaged decking or flashing takes longer than a straightforward tear-off.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6,
              7,
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Scheduling & Permits: Getting on a contractor's schedule, ordering specialty materials, or handling insurance claims can add days or weeks before work begins.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              9,
              10
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your roofing material, approximate roof size or stories, and whether you are working through insurance , I can give you a more tailored estimate."
      }
    ],
